    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), our premier start as he faces a favorable matchup against a struggling starter with an xERA of 5.20. His elite score is bolstered by a potent mix of park factors and the optimal lead-off spot. Following closely is **Kyle Tucker** (76.77), whose production remains high despite a tougher matchup, largely due to his ability to mitigate platoon disadvantages. **Andy Pages** (73.34) also earns high marks today; while he faces an elite catcher behind the dish, the combination of his #2 spot in the order and a favorable park environment makes him a standout play. **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas** also offer excellent value, with **Miguel Vargas** specifically benefiting from a high xERA opposing starter and positive wind conditions that could turn fly balls into crucial home runs.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nolan Schanuel** (45.47), who was the first cut from the starting nine. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects as a solid contributor, the optimizer leaned toward the speed-oriented profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg**, prioritizing their dynamic stolen base potential in a category that remains our primary scarcity concern. **Nasim Nunez** (47.71) earned his spot despite a challenging SP matchup specifically because of a slow delivery from Early, which provides a high-leverage opportunity for a swipe. \n\nWe must remain cautious with **Josh Lowe** (47.45) and **Jackson Merrill** (47.12), as both are hovering near the floor of our starting criteria. **Josh Lowe** is battling a suppressed expectation due to an unfavorable park and a strong pitcher, while **Jackson Merrill** faces a lefty specialist who excels at holding runners, significantly blunting his utility in our 5x5 build. As we await final confirmation on **Josh Lowe**'s lineup placement, we are keeping a close watch on the weather and any late-breaking news regarding our remaining active slots. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our only major injury-related vacancy, keeping our focus strictly on the healthy, high-sprint-speed options currently in play.",
